.TH tapectl-cartridge-edit 1  "tapectl-cartridge-edit " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-cartridge\-edit \- Correct a registered cartridge\*(Aqs generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl cartridge edit\fR <\fB\-\-generation\fR> [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBARCODE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Correct a registered cartridge\*(Aqs generation
.PP
ADR\-0012, *Rulings recorded as consequences*: "`cartridge edit \-\-generation` corrects a wrong generation (Tier 1: it is a fact correction, and the wrong\-medium check at the next init still applies)." Tier 1 under ADR\-0008 — no prompt, no `\-\-force`, no `\-\-yes`, and it applies to every status, `retired_permanent` included. This edits only the `cartridges` row: it never rewrites `volumes.media_type` or `volumes.capacity_bytes` (ADR\-0010 decision 3 — capacity is decided once at init and stored on the volume).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
The cartridge\*(Aqs corrected generation (e.g. LTO\-5, LTO\-6, LTO\-7\-M8)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIBARCODE\fR>
